Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-15-2000||05:06 PM||||Well, I was dumping several buckets of water in my system to see if it was all good, and I looked under the car to see that the left rear hose was not connected..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Did that, then filled it up again, and it started pouring out around the drain plug. I felt around the drain plug, and it was dry, and the hoses were all connected, but I went in for a closer inspection and it looks like there is another small hole(tube) out the bottom of the drain plug.. Whats that for, and shouldn't the plug have stopped it? It wouldn't stop turning.. I hope it's the plug that is stripped and not the actual hole (didn't turn bad, still required a bunch of force). But, I'll assume for now (until one of you guys tells me otherwise) that I need a new plug. Can I get that at a parts shop, or is it strictly a dealer thing? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-15-2000||07:21 PM||||I was in a advance auto the other day. they had a whole bunch on a shelf. I don't know with one Fiero uses but I expect you can get it at the parts store.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kevin-84SE||11-15-2000||09:03 PM||||Try pushing in and turning, maybe the threads of the drain plug are out of the threads in the radiator, I think when I changed the coolant in mine, I had to push in and turn to tighten the radiator drain plug. <P>   Kevin||||reg||1
